# Loaded by Nx for every `test` target (local `nx test` / `nx run-many -t test`), after the project's own `.env.test`.
# Nest 12 and other dependencies are ESM-only: Jest loads them as native modules, which Node offers to it only
# behind this flag. The Angular projects must run WITHOUT it, so each one has a `.env.test` of its own that clears
# NODE_OPTIONS (a project's file wins: Nx loads it first, and the first value of a variable is kept). CI does the
# same split in .github/workflows/test-unit.yml (it turns .env loading off). See jest.patterns.js.
NODE_OPTIONS=--experimental-vm-modules
